wide|PASS: Side-to-side dimension and table-through-doorway example support rộng rather than tall or deep. Comparative forms and a metre wide are grammatical. Vietnamese passive movement through the opening preserves the original outcome.
bible|REVIEW: [FORM] Christian sacred collection and physical-copy example are supported without asserting religious claims as history. Kinh Thánh is appropriate. displayFormProposal defaults to lowercase bible in the parser; add a Bible display overlay while preserving the normalized identity and manuscript bytes.
federation|PASS: Organizational union and state-government union are genuinely different source-supported boundaries; club federation and fictional states avoid the source's inaccurate real-organization example. Vietnamese liên đoàn versus liên bang is precise. Shared central power and retained member independence distinguish a federation from any loose international group.
morals|PASS: Principles of right/wrong and personal choice fit plural morals. Vietnamese các nguyên tắc đạo đức avoids confusing morals with a story's lesson. Neutral fictional example avoids repeating the source's stigmatizing claim about a group of people.
quite|REVIEW: [POS_CLASSIFICATION] Both actual adverb meanings are supported by Oxford and accessible Cambridge grammar text: gradable spacious and complete correct. The 4600 source labels quite ADJECTIVE; that conflicting classification remains unresolved rather than adopted. Context/intonation/region affect degree, so no approved CEFR or universal strength is inferred.
